{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Noah came in, and Shem and Ham and Japheth, the sons of Noah, and Noah's wife.</b> It would have been fitting to say 'Noah came in, and Shem and Ham and Japheth his sons, and his wife and the three wives of his sons,' but Scripture always mentions him by name, as a token of fondness. It is the way of the world that a person mentions his beloved by name always, when he finds favor in his eyes — all the more so Noah, who found favor in the eyes of HaShem."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:57.630809552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}